WEBVTT

00:00:00.476 --> 00:00:04.018
Open FinBuddy and choose Try the demo.

00:00:04.018 --> 00:00:08.647
The sample household shows income
received, money spent and the bills

00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:07.933
still due this month.

00:00:08.329 --> 00:00:11.375
You can explore without an account.

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:15.136
We’ll switch to a fictional signed-in
household to record a month of

00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:14.327
its own.

00:00:15.356 --> 00:00:19.125
Asha has received eighty thousand
rupees.

00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:24.154
On Home, she chooses Add income, enters
the amount and calls it

00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:22.843
Salary.

00:00:23.239 --> 00:00:29.068
After she saves, Left after bills shows
eighty thousand rupees.

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:31.272
This is income she has received, so she
can plan with it now.

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:37.952
In Expenses, Asha adds twelve hundred
and fifty rupees, chooses Food

00:00:37.952 --> 00:00:42.010
and Dining, and writes Weekly
groceries.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.063
More details lets her add a person,
platform or receipt.

00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:47.559
She saves, then reopens Expenses.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:52.043
The groceries are still there, and the
monthly expense total includes

00:00:52.043 --> 00:00:50.931
the purchase.

00:00:51.956 --> 00:00:56.841
Asha adds her nine hundred rupee
internet bill, sets it to repeat

00:00:56.841 --> 00:01:00.258
monthly and saves it. In Manage bills,
she selects Record payment.

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:04.285
Saving the payment adds it to Expenses.

00:01:04.285 --> 00:01:08.618
Groceries and internet now total two
thousand one hundred and fifty

00:01:08.618 --> 00:01:14.261
rupees. If she had already logged the
expense, she could link it

00:01:14.261 --> 00:01:11.590
instead.

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:17.913
Overview shows the daily average,
largest expense, top category and

00:01:17.913 --> 00:01:21.493
comparison with last month. Here,
groceries are the largest expense.

00:01:21.889 --> 00:01:26.939
If a category looks high, open the
underlying expenses before deciding

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:27.741
whether to change its monthly budget.

00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:34.268
Under Savings, Asha records the latest
value of her emergency fund,

00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:37.303
fifty thousand rupees. She can enter
the date she checked the balance.

00:01:37.699 --> 00:01:42.715
Next time she checks, she updates the
same holding.

00:01:42.715 --> 00:01:46.525
It stays separate from the income and
expenses she recorded this

00:01:46.525 --> 00:01:45.081
month.

00:01:46.116 --> 00:01:49.795
Now try FinVision with the public
sample.

00:01:49.795 --> 00:01:54.101
Add a school-fees goal of one lakh
twenty thousand rupees and choose

00:01:54.101 --> 00:01:54.528
May twenty twenty-eight as its target
month.

00:01:54.924 --> 00:01:58.493
Select the new goal to see its outlook.

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:01.580
This example starts at zero.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.766
In your own plan, you can link savings
you have already set aside.

00:02:04.796 --> 00:02:09.702
Add a recurring deposit for five
thousand rupees per month.

00:02:09.702 --> 00:02:13.918
Choose January twenty twenty-seven as
the first month, twelve

00:02:13.918 --> 00:02:15.082
instalments and an annual interest
estimate of seven percent.

00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:19.667
The preview separates sixty thousand
rupees in deposits from the

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.636
interest estimate. Save the schedule to
include it in the goal.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:27.610
The projected balance is sixty-two
thousand three hundred and ten

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:33.404
rupees and sixty-six paise. The
remaining gap is fifty-seven thousand

00:02:33.404 --> 00:02:33.907
six hundred and eighty-nine rupees and
thirty-four paise.

00:02:34.303 --> 00:02:38.961
Open See the balance along the way for
the dates and estimates.

00:02:38.961 --> 00:02:42.750
You can change the deposit or the
deadline and see whether the goal

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:42.000
becomes achievable.

00:02:43.036 --> 00:02:48.203
Settings holds the appearance choices
and, for signed-in accounts,

00:02:48.203 --> 00:02:53.536
Developer Options. The technical guide
explains how a scoped token

00:02:53.536 --> 00:02:52.313
works with the API.

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:57.160
To try the same journey, open the
sample household or the FinVision

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.721
demo. Sign in when you want to keep
your own records.
